HTTPRequest
Inherits: Node → Object
Description
The HTTPRequest node is used to perform HTTP requests to download or upload data from/to a web server. It supports GET, POST, PUT, DELETE and other HTTP methods. This node automatically handles redirects and can store cookies if needed.
Tutorial
To use HTTPRequest, add it to your scene tree or create it via script. Connect the request_completed signal to receive responses:
func _ready():
    $HTTPRequest.request("https://api.example.com/data")

func _on_HTTPRequest_request_completed(result, response_code, headers, body):
    if result == HTTPRequest.RESULT_SUCCESS and response_code == 200:
        var json = parse_json(body.get_string_from_utf8())
        print(json)
